Compile/run:
     - Compile using
            make
     - run executable with
            ./gerp inputDirectory outputFile";

Purpose
    Implementation of the phaseOne functions, which help to remove all 
    non-alphanumeric characters from strings to make them 'words' and traverse
    directories to recursively output all files within it.

Acknowledgements
    Special thanks to the Peter Morganelli, the TA who did out design checkoff
    and help clarify some parts of the project where our approach was going to
    be more difficult than necessary to implement or fully ineffective.

Files:

    Processing.cpp: Implementation of the phaseOne functions, which help to 
        remove all non-alphanumeric characters from strings to make them 
        'words' and traverse directories to recursively output all files within 
        it.

    Processing.h: Acts as the interface for the processing functions of Gerp. 
        This is meant for use by an outside user with little to no programming 
        knowledge. 

    README:
        Acts as a way to navigate and understand the program as a whole 
        including details on architectural and data structure design.

    unit_test.h:
        Contains unit tests for various program functionalities, ensuring 
        correctness.

    Makefile:
        Automates the compilation process for the program.


Architectural Overview:
    There is no architecture as of yet outside of processing.h and 
    processing.cpp which includes it. The bulk of the design will be 
    implemented during phase 2 of this project.

Data Structures and Algorithms:
    This traverseDirectory recursively moves throughout FSTrees using DirNodes.
    More data structures and algorithms will be added during phase two of this
    project.

Testing
    The first phase testing for this project including using unit tests 
    implemented in unit_test.h. This testing covered the efficacy and 
    constistency of the stripNonAlphaNum() function. All tests were executed, 
    and assertions were used to validate expected outcomes. These tests ensure 
    the correctness and accuracy of these process could be trusted for latter 
    portion of this project. Additionally, traverseDirectory() was tested using
    expected results with diff.
    
Part that you found most difficult:
    The traversing of the trees was a little bit tricky simply because it
    required a solid understanding of the spec to implement properly

Time Spent: 4 hours
